# 3. USER ROLES AND ADMIN PERMISSIONS

## 3.1 Platform Roles

The existing roles are:

- ADMIN
- CONTRACTOR
- CUSTOMER

Phase 10 must preserve the existing role system.

Do not introduce a new role system without an approved requirement.

## 3.2 Admin Access

Admin users can access authorized administrative modules.

The backend must verify Admin permissions on every protected API request.

Hiding a frontend button is not authorization.

## 3.3 Customer Permissions

Customers must not access administrative functionality.

Customers must only access their own:

- Profile.
- Decks.
- Uploaded photographs.
- Estimates.
- Leads and enquiries.
- Authorized AI analysis records.

## 3.4 Contractor Permissions

Contractors must not access administrative functionality.

Contractors must only access their authorized:

- Profile.
- Verification records.
- Assigned leads.
- Authorized deck information.
- Estimates.
- Discount information.
- Commission records.

## 3.5 Admin Account Protection

The following operations require special protection:

- Changing Admin roles.
- Disabling an Admin account.
- Deleting an Admin account.
- Changing security-related configuration.
- Changing platform-wide financial configuration.

Never allow an Admin to accidentally remove the last usable administrative account.

Sensitive actions should require confirmation and must be audited.

