# 5. USER MANAGEMENT

## 5.1 Objective

Admin must have a centralized interface to manage registered platform users.

This includes customers, contractors, and administrative accounts, subject to the security restrictions defined in this specification.

## 5.2 User List

Display:

- User ID.
- Name.
- Email.
- Phone number, if available.
- Role.
- Account status.
- Registration date.
- Last login, if tracked.
- Last updated date.

## 5.3 User CRUD

### Create

Admin may create users only through an explicitly supported and secure workflow.

Requirements:

- Validate all required fields.
- Validate email uniqueness.
- Validate phone uniqueness where required by existing rules.
- Assign only permitted roles.
- Never allow arbitrary role escalation.
- Never store plain-text passwords.
- Use the existing authentication and password hashing implementation.

If an invitation or password setup process is not implemented, do not create an unsafe alternative.

### Read

Admin can:

- View user lists.
- Search users.
- Filter by role.
- Filter by account status.
- View individual user details.
- View permitted related records.

Sensitive information must be protected.

### Update

Admin can update permitted user information.

Possible fields:

- Name.
- Contact details.
- Account status.
- Other approved profile fields.

Role changes must follow strict authorization rules.

Never allow modification of:

- Password hashes.
- Authentication tokens.
- Internal security fields.
- Immutable audit information.

### Delete / Deactivate

Do not permanently delete users who own decks, estimates, leads, commissions, verification documents, or financial history.

Use account deactivation, suspension, or archival according to the existing data lifecycle.

Permanent deletion should only be allowed when data retention and dependency checks establish that it is safe and legally permitted.

## 5.4 User Status Management

Use existing account statuses.

Admin should be able to:

- View status.
- Activate or deactivate an account.
- Suspend an account if supported.
- Record a reason for sensitive status changes.

The backend must enforce valid transitions.

