1. Dashboard
2. User Management
3. Customer Management
4. Contractor Management
5. Deck Management
6. Estimate Management
7. Lead Management
8. AI Analysis
9. Material Catalog
10. Service Catalog
11. Pricing Configuration
12. Discounts
13. Commissions
14. Reports and Analytics
15. Platform Settings
16. Audit Logs

Organize related sections into groups where appropriate.

## 19.2 Reusable UI Components

Use reusable components for:

- Data tables.
- Search fields.
- Filters.
- Pagination.
- Status badges.
- Detail panels.
- Forms.
- Confirmation dialogs.
- Delete/deactivation confirmation.
- Loading indicators.
- Error messages.
- Empty states.
- Export controls.

Do not duplicate the same table and CRUD implementation in every module.

## 19.3 CRUD Interface Requirements

Every editable module must provide the required operations.

### Create

- Form opens correctly.
- Fields are validated.
- Submission reaches the backend.
- Loading state is displayed.
- Success response updates the UI.
- Errors are displayed clearly.

### Read

- List loads from the backend.
- Detail view loads the correct record.
- Search works.
- Filters work.
- Pagination works.
- Empty state works.

### Update

- Existing data loads into the form.
- Validation runs.
- Only permitted fields are submitted.
- Backend changes are persisted.
- UI reflects the saved data.
- Errors are handled.

### Delete / Deactivate

- Confirmation is displayed.
- Backend verifies dependencies and permissions.
- Destructive actions are blocked when unsafe.
- Appropriate deactivation or archival is used.
- UI reflects the actual result.

## 19.4 UI Reliability

Every page must handle:

- Loading.
- Success.
- Validation errors.
- Authorization errors.
- Not-found responses.
- Network failures.
- Empty datasets.
- Expired sessions.

No dead buttons.

No fake success notifications.

No placeholder charts presented as real data.

No forms that only update local component state without saving to the backend.

