# 23. TESTING STRATEGY

Phase 10 requires more extensive testing than a normal UI-only feature.

Every module must be tested at multiple levels.

## 23.1 Backend Unit Tests

Test:

- Validation.
- Service methods.
- Permission checks.
- Business rules.
- Status transitions.
- Aggregation calculations.
- Dependency checks.

## 23.2 Backend Integration Tests

Test complete API workflows.

For every supported CRUD module:

### Create Tests

- Authorized Admin creates a valid record.
- Invalid input is rejected.
- Duplicate records are rejected.
- Non-admin access is denied.
- Database persistence is verified.

### Read Tests

- Authorized Admin can retrieve records.
- Search works.
- Filters work.
- Pagination works.
- Invalid IDs are handled.
- Unauthorized users cannot access Admin records.

### Update Tests

- Valid update is persisted.
- Invalid update is rejected.
- Protected fields cannot be modified.
- Historical data is preserved.
- Failed updates do not corrupt records.

### Delete / Deactivate Tests

- Valid deactivation works.
- Dependency restrictions work.
- Financial and audit history is preserved.
- Unauthorized deletion is rejected.
- Repeated requests behave safely.

